        "original_id": "df66acec-1230-5d84-abf3-573ffa30926e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Millbrook, Chalfont, Northeast Philadelphia, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States, Bensalem, Bucks County, Center City\n- Products: Philadelphia Mills, Franklin Mills\n- Concepts: neighbourhood, enclosed shopping mall\n\nFacts:\n- Millbrook, also known as Chalfont, is a neighbourhood in the Northeast section of Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States.\n- Philadelphia Mills, formerly called Franklin Mills, is an enclosed shopping mall in Northeast Philadelphia that borders Bensalem in Bucks County and is 15 miles outside Center City.\n- Philadelphia Mills was formerly named for Benjamin Franklin.\n- In 2006, Philadelphia Mills had about 200 stores, a movie theatre, two food courts, and seven theme restaurants, and it received an estimated 18 million visitors.",
